rs/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-03T11:01:17Z","updated_at":"2026-01-03T12:17:17Z","body":"Here :D\r\n[joypad-info-test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24414989/joypad-info-test.zip)\r\n\r\nAnd I just found a web page with Steam Deck's buttons and their names, so we will use it to get more specific button names. https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2804823261&ysclid=mjy9ogdptd46361097\r\n\r\nMay I ask if you can test the project above, verify that the model name is \"Steam Deck\", press every button on the Steam Deck that is usable in games and save the reported names for them that are shown in \"Last pressed button\" label?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3706975956/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3707258215","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112680#issuecomment-3707258215","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112680","id":3707258215,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7c-EVn","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-03T18:24:16Z","updated_at":"2026-01-03T18:24:16Z","body":"I decided to use `thirdparty/sdl/joystick/controller_type.h` and `thirdparty/sdl/joystick/controller_list.h` directly instead of relying on `SDL_GetGamepadType()` so that we can use `Input.get_joy_model()` and `Input.get_joy_scheme()` on platforms where SDL support is not currently planned, i.e. Android and web. We should be able to use these headers there since they don't use other SDL code/headers.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3707258215/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3906267153","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112680#issuecomment-3906267153","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112680","id":3906267153,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7o1OgR","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-16T03:37:13Z","updated_at":"2026-02-16T04:40:58Z","body":"I might move the buttons/axes names into a separate PR, I think I have a better way to make this functionality\nI thought about something like `Input.get_action_input_names(device = -1)` that allows the developer to retrieve the button/axis names (not IDs) from input actions, and the names will depend on the joypad's model and scheme.\nBasically, if there are keyboard buttons and joypad buttons in an action, this method would return keyboard button names if the last used device wasn't a joypad, and joypad button names otherwise.\nGetting button IDs makes sense, but they're separate enums, so multiple methods would have to be created, and I think `InputMap.action_get_events()` (I hope I got the name right) is better suited for this.\n\nOr it might make sense to let the developers themselves provide the buttons/axes names based on the joypad model.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3906267153/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4076851987","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112680#issuecomment-4076851987","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112680","id":4076851987,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7y_9MT","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-17T17:49:49Z","updated_at":"2026-03-17T17:49:49Z","body":"I was thinking about writing a proposal for this PR (specifically, for battery and connection information), but now that I think about it, these methods might not be useful for games, since I currently can't find an example of games that use those and I currently can't think of a good reason to use those in a game, in which case I might remove these features from this PR (unless we can find a good reason for them to exist in Godot).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4076851987/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4076961740","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112680#issuecomment-4076961740","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112680","id":4076961740,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zAX_M","user":{"login":"autione","id":28675903,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Njc1OTAz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28675903?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/autione","html_url":"https://github.com/autione","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/autione/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/autione/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/autione/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/autione/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/autione/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/autione/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/autione/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/autione/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/autione/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-17T18:05:11Z","updated_at":"2026-03-17T18:05:11Z","body":"Would it be too harmful to keep them though? If it's not too costly, then I personally think there would be no downsides to keeping these methods available for those few who can find a use for it.\r\n\r\nConsider that Godot is also used for things beyond just games, like desktop apps or even development tools as well. For example, if someone is developing a gamepad tester/viewer, or a launcher app, or anything that would benefit from visual display of this queried info.\r\n\r\nWhereas for games, I can imagine being able to query battery info coming in handy to let the player know their controller is low on battery, then pausing the game or suggesting them to save their progress, plug the controller in or switch controllers.\r\n\r\nSimilarly for connection information, if I understood what it means correctly, games could use that to warn about features that won't work over a wireless connection, for example. Some games on Steam do that already, especially if they use fancy hardware-specific capabilities that only work through USB or whatnot.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4076961740/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4076981985","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112680#issuecomment-4076981985","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112680","id":4076981985,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zAc7h","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":fa